  "summary": "I wrote the whole scene in `src/main.ts`, but I couldn't confirm that it renders or that the Aura3D material options are valid. `node_modules/@aura3d/` is empty in this sandbox. `typecheck` reports only `Cannot find module '@aura3d/engine'`, and I never saw a frame. I wrote the engine calls from `docs/agents/api-signatures.md`, `docs/agents/recipes.md` and the recipe sources.\n\n- **Floor and backdrop:** a custom mesh with a flat floor, a 4.5-unit radius curve and a vertical wall, so the floor runs seamlessly into the backdrop. It is light grey and receives shadows.\n- **Spheres:** three equal spheres (radius 0.8) in a row, all built from one procedural sphere generator.\n  - **Glass:** `material.physical` with transmission 1, IOR 1.5, a pale tint, opacity 0.5 and a full clearcoat, so it has highlights and reflects the studio environment.\n  - **Brushed metal:** fully metallic, roughness 0.34 and anisotropy 0.85. Fine concentric streaks are baked into the vertex colours, so the reflection looks stretched and blurred.\n  - **Fabric (dark red wool):** roughness 1, no metal and sheen 1. A plain-weave pattern is baked in as both vertex-colour tone and real surface displacement, with normals recomputed so the threads catch light.\n- **Lighting:**\n  - **Key:** a shadow-casting warm directional light.\n  - **Fill:** a dimmer cool light on the opposite side.\n  - **Rim:** a light from behind.\n  - **Other light:** `environments.studio` for reflections, a faint hemisphere light, and contact shadows plus ambient occlusion and a light bloom.\n  - **Key animation:** the key light drifts along x as `4.5·sin(0.4t)` every frame.\n- **Camera and state:** the camera is fixed, slightly raised and three-quarter-front, with all three spheres in frame. `window.__TASK_STATE__` holds the three sphere names and the live `keyLightX`. `__EVAL_READY__` is set after the engine reports ready and two animation frames have passed.\n\nSome material fields (`transmission`, `ior`, `th